From e2f2c1af72c9f8284a2c752d3cc4358ff09d881d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "nonggia.liang" <nonggia@192.168.0.101>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 15:54:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] feat(catalog-lakehouse-cust): scaffold cust catalog with
 JDBC backend

Register a new `cust` provider (catalog-a) that will mirror an upstream
Iceberg catalog (catalog-b) with copy-on-write semantics. This is the
PR 1 scaffolding milestone of the implementation plan documented in
spec.md:

- Add the new `catalog-lakehouse-cust` Gradle module and register it in
  settings.gradle.kts.
- `CustCatalog` extends `IcebergCatalog` and reports `shortName()="cust"`;
  resolvable via SPI through `META-INF/services/org.apache.gravitino.CatalogProvider`.
- `CustCatalogPropertiesMetadata` extends the Iceberg catalog property
  metadata and adds the required `upstream-catalog` property.
- `CustCatalogOperations` extends `IcebergCatalogOperations` and forces
  `catalog-backend=JDBC` regardless of the caller-supplied value, so
  catalog-a inherits JdbcCatalog's CAS for atomic commit.
- Add the `CUST` enum value to `IcebergCatalogBackend`.
- Relax `DynamicIcebergConfigProvider` to accept both `lakehouse-iceberg`
  and `cust` providers so cust catalogs can be served via the Iceberg
  REST Server's dynamic config path.

Mirror/COW behaviors (load forwarding, location rewriting, first-write
materialization) are intentionally out of scope and will be added in
subsequent PRs. At this stage the cust catalog behaves like a plain
JDBC-backed Iceberg catalog.

14 unit tests cover SPI resolution, property metadata inheritance, the
forced JDBC backend override, and SQLite-backed end-to-end initialize.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
