Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 21:43:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] feat(catalog-lakehouse-cust): add CustIcebergCatalog with
 unmaterialized mirror reads

PR 2 of the cust catalog implementation. Adds the catalog-a Iceberg Catalog
that serves reads of unmaterialized mirror tables by proxying to the upstream
catalog-b with location rewriting.

Key additions:
- CustIcebergCatalog: extends JdbcCatalogWithMetadataLocationSupport with
  loadTable/tableExists/listTables routing. Falls through to catalog-b on
  NoSuchTableException, rewrites the upstream metadata location to the local
  warehouse, and wraps the result in CustReadOnlyTableOperations.
- CustMetadataRewriter: produces a new TableMetadata with the top-level
  location and path-style properties (write.metadata.path, write.data.path)
  rewritten to the catalog-a warehouse; manifest/data-file paths inside
  snapshots are intentionally preserved.
- CustReadOnlyTableOperations: read-only TableOperations for mirror reads;
  commit() throws UnsupportedOperationException (first-write materialization
  is implemented in PR 3).
- UpstreamLookup + UpstreamLookupHolder: side channel for the REST server to
  register the upstream catalog resolver without the cust module taking a
  compile-time dependency on iceberg-rest-server.
- IcebergCatalogUtil.loadCustCatalog: reflection-based instantiation via
  Iceberg CatalogUtil.loadCatalog to avoid a circular module dependency.
- CustCatalogPropertiesMetadata.transformProperties: override to re-inject
  upstream-catalog past the toIcebergCatalogProperties allow-list filter.

Tests: 18 new unit tests (TestCustIcebergCatalog, TestCustMetadataRewriter)
plus updated TestCustCatalogOperations; 32 cust-module tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
