+ *
+ * <h2>Read path</h2>
+ *
+ * {@link #current()} and {@link #refresh()} return {@code upstreamBase}. This lets clients scan the
+ * upstream data files (the manifest-list URIs inside {@code upstreamBase}'s snapshots still point
+ * at catalog-b's storage; per spec §1, catalog-a clients have read access to catalog-b).
+ *
+ * <h2>Commit path (first-write materialization)</h2>
+ *
+ * Iceberg's commit machinery calls {@link #commit(TableMetadata, TableMetadata)} with {@code base =
+ * current() = upstreamBase} and {@code newMetadata} built on top of {@code upstreamBase} (typically
+ * via {@code AppendFiles}). We delegate to {@code localOps.commit(null, newMetadata)} — passing
+ * {@code null} for {@code base} is what tells the underlying {@code JdbcCatalog} to take its
+ * <em>create-table</em> (INSERT) code path rather than its update-table code path.
+ *
+ * <p>Risk mitigation (spec §8.8): JdbcCatalog's {@code BaseMetastoreTableOperations.commit} rejects
+ * a non-null {@code base} when the table row does not exist. So we cannot forward the upstream
+ * metadata as {@code base}; we must pass {@code null} and let {@code newMetadata} (which already
+ * incorporates the upstream snapshot chain via the client's append operation) become the first
+ * committed state.
+ *
+ * <h2>Concurrency</h2>
+ *
+ * The local {@code JdbcCatalog} provides row-level CAS via the {@code iceberg_tables} INSERT
+ * constraint. Concurrent first-writers race on the INSERT; only one succeeds, the others get {@code
+ * AlreadyExistsException} wrapped as {@code CommitFailedException} by {@code
+ * BaseMetastoreTableOperations}. The CAS handling for concurrent first-write is exercised in PR 4;
+ * this class itself does not add additional locking.
+ *
+ * <h2>Post-materialization</h2>
+ *
+ * Once the local table exists, subsequent {@link CustIcebergCatalog#loadTable} calls take the
+ * materialized branch ({@code super.loadTable}) and return a standard {@code JdbcTableOperations} —
+ * clients that hold a stale {@code CustTableOperations} reference after a successful commit will
+ * get {@code AlreadyExistsException} on any further commit attempt, which is the correct Iceberg
+ * semantics telling them to reload.
+ */
+final class CustTableOperations implements TableOperations {
+
+  private static final Logger LOG = LoggerFactory.getLogger(CustTableOperations.class);
+
+  private final TableOperations localOps;
+  private final TableMetadata upstreamBase;
+  private final FileIO upstreamIo;
+
+  /**
+   * Constructs a CustTableOperations.
+   *
+   * @param localOps a fresh {@link TableOperations} from the underlying {@code JdbcCatalog} for
+   *     {@code identifier}; obtained by {@link CustIcebergCatalog} via {@code
+   *     super.newTableOps(ident)}.
+   * @param upstreamBase the upstream table's metadata with location already rewritten to the
+   *     catalog-a warehouse.
+   * @param upstreamIo the upstream table's {@link FileIO}; used for reads of upstream manifests and
+   *     data files.
+   */
+  CustTableOperations(TableOperations localOps, TableMetadata upstreamBase, FileIO upstreamIo) {
+    this.localOps = localOps;
+    this.upstreamBase = upstreamBase;
+    this.upstreamIo = upstreamIo;
+  }
+
+  /**
+   * Returns the upstream metadata (rewritten to local warehouse). Clients use this to scan the
+   * upstream data files; the commit machinery uses this as the {@code base} for building {@code
+   * newMetadata}.
+   */
+  @Override
+  public TableMetadata current() {
+    return upstreamBase;
+  }
+
+  /**
+   * Returns the same metadata as {@link #current()}. This is a point-in-time snapshot of the
+   * upstream state captured when {@link CustIcebergCatalog#loadTable} was called; we deliberately
+   * do not re-fetch from catalog-b on refresh. Clients wanting the latest upstream state should
+   * call {@code loadTable} again.
+   */
+  @Override
+  public TableMetadata refresh() {
+    return upstreamBase;
+  }
+
+  /**
+   * First-write materialization: delegates to the local {@code JdbcCatalog}'s {@code
+   * TableOperations.commit} with {@code base = null} so the underlying {@code JdbcCatalog} takes
+   * its create-table (INSERT) path and writes a new metadata.json anchored at the rewritten
+   * (catalog-a) location.
+   *
+   * <p>The {@code base} argument from Iceberg's commit machinery is intentionally ignored: it
+   * equals {@code upstreamBase} (our {@link #current()}), but the local JDBC backend has no row for
+   * this table yet, so passing it would cause {@code BaseMetastoreTableOperations.commit} to throw
+   * {@code CommitFailedException} ("stale table metadata"). The {@code newMetadata} argument
+   * already incorporates the upstream snapshot chain because the client built it on top of the
+   * metadata they received from {@link CustIcebergCatalog#loadTable}.
+   *
+   * @throws org.apache.iceberg.exceptions.AlreadyExistsException if another writer materialized the
+   *     table between our loadTable and this commit (CAS failure)
+   */
+  @Override
+  public void commit(TableMetadata base, TableMetadata newMetadata) {
+    LOG.info(
+        "First-write materialization: delegating to local JdbcCatalog with base=null, "
+            + "newMetadata location={}",
+        newMetadata.location());
+    localOps.commit(null, newMetadata);
+  }
+
+  /**
+   * Returns the upstream {@link FileIO}. Per spec §1, the deployment ensures catalog-a clients (and
+   * the REST server) can read from catalog-b's storage, so the upstream FileIO can read existing
+   * manifests and data files.
+   */
+  @Override
+  public FileIO io() {
+    return upstreamIo;
+  }
+
+  /**
+   * Delegates to the local ops. This method is consulted by Iceberg when it needs to compute a
+   * metadata file path for new commits; for the first-write case the local {@code JdbcCatalog}'s
+   * implementation produces paths under the local warehouse.
+   */
+  @Override
+  public String metadataFileLocation(String fileName) {
+    return localOps.metadataFileLocation(fileName);
+  }
+
+  /**
+   * Delegates to the local ops so that any new data/metadata files written during commit land under
+   * the catalog-a warehouse.
+   */
+  @Override
+  public LocationProvider locationProvider() {
+    return localOps.locationProvider();
+  }
+}
