From 287c75f35baacc19f60aa7c02db759298969598e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "nonggia.liang" <nonggia@192.168.0.101>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 22:22:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] feat(catalog-lakehouse-cust): add concurrent first-write
 CAS handling
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PR 4 of the cust catalog implementation. Verifies spec §5.2.2 and §10:
among multiple concurrent first-write attempts on the same unmaterialized
mirror table, exactly one wins and the rest receive the standard Iceberg
conflict signal (CommitFailedException).

Changes to CustTableOperations.commit:
- Pre-check via localOps.current(): fail fast with CommitFailedException
  if another writer already materialized the table, avoiding a wasted
  JDBC INSERT.
- Wrap AlreadyExistsException as CommitFailedException: the underlying
  JdbcCatalog throws AlreadyExistsException when the JDBC UNIQUE
  constraint catches a race inside doCommit (or from the early
  base != current() check in BaseMetastoreTableOperations.commit). Per
  spec §10, surfacing this as CommitFailedException ensures the
  CatalogHandlers.commit retry machinery and standard Iceberg clients
  handle it correctly.

Test setup fix:
- Switched TestCustCommit's SQLite URI from :memory: to file-based
  (jdbc:sqlite:<tempDir>/cust-test.db). SQLite's :memory: creates a
  private DB per connection, which broke the concurrent test where
  multiple pool connections must share state (some connections saw
  "no such table: iceberg_tables").

New tests:
- testConcurrentFirstMaterialize: pre-loads N=8 independent
  CustTableOperations, races their commits via ExecutorService, asserts
  1 success + 7 CommitFailedException, verifies the table is observable
  as materialized after the race.
- testRetryAfterConflictSeesMaterialized: A and B both load the
  unmaterialized mirror before either commits; A wins, B's stale
  CustTableOperations throws CommitFailedException; B retries via
  reload and the standard update path succeeds.

36 cust-module tests pass (was 34 in PR 3).

Out of scope: HTTP 409 Conflict integration test (PR 7), production
UpstreamLookupHolder wiring (PR 7).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
