From 075a82a949b4a67022fd0aa1681ffd23deacb9b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "nonggia.liang" <nonggia@192.168.0.101>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 10:00:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] feat(catalog-lakehouse-cust): add metrics and audit
 events
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implement spec §5.6 observability with 4 counters and 3 event types:

Metrics (CustMetricsSource via MetricsSystem):
- cust.mirror.reads, cust.upstream.fwd.reads on upstream fallthrough
- cust.materialize.events on successful first-write
- cust.conflict.counts on CAS race loss

Events (via EventBus):
- CustMirrorReadEvent on unmaterialized mirror load
- CustMaterializeEvent on first-write materialization
- CustConflictEvent on concurrent CAS conflict

CustObservabilityHolder provides static injection (same pattern as
UpstreamLookupHolder). CustObservability facade wraps metrics + events
per catalog instance with null-safe no-ops. Add TestCustMetrics (3
tests) and TestCustEvents (5 tests). All 53 module tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
