+# Catalog-Lakehouse-Cust
+
+A custom Iceberg catalog type that mirrors an upstream Iceberg catalog with copy-on-write (COW)
+semantics. It provides transparent read access to upstream tables while allowing independent
+writes that materialize tables locally.
+
+## Overview
+
+The `cust` catalog (catalog-a) sits in front of a standard Iceberg catalog (catalog-b) and adds
+three capabilities:
+
+1. **Transparent mirror reads**: Tables that exist in catalog-b but not yet in catalog-a are
+   served transparently — the upstream metadata location is rewritten to the catalog-a warehouse
+   so clients see a unified view.
+2. **First-write materialization**: The first write to an unmaterialized mirror table creates a
+   local JDBC entry with the committed snapshot, establishing an independent copy.
+3. **Post-materialization independence**: Once materialized, the table is fully decoupled from
+   the upstream — subsequent reads and writes go through the local JDBC backend only.
+
+## Deployment Prerequisites
+
+| Requirement | Detail |
+|---|---|
+| **Same metalake** | catalog-a and catalog-b must be in the same Gravitino metalake. |
+| **Same REST Server** | Both catalogs are served by the same Iceberg REST Server instance (no cross-process auth). |
+| **Storage read access** | catalog-a clients (and the REST server) must have **read** access to catalog-b's storage (manifest files, data files). |
+| **JDBC backend** | catalog-a uses a JDBC database (SQLite, PostgreSQL, or MySQL) for its metadata store. |
+| **catalog-b exists** | catalog-b must be created before the first read through catalog-a. It need not exist at catalog-a creation time — resolution is lazy. |
+
+## Configuration
+
+### Creating catalog-a
+
+```bash
+# 1. Create catalog-b (standard Iceberg catalog with JDBC backend)
+curl -X POST http://localhost:8090/api/metalakes/my_metalake/catalogs \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{
+    "name": "catalog-b",
+    "type": "RELATIONAL",
+    "provider": "lakehouse-iceberg",
+    "comment": "Upstream Iceberg catalog",
+    "properties": {
+      "catalog-backend": "jdbc",
+      "uri": "jdbc:postgresql://db:5432/iceberg_b",
+      "warehouse": "s3://bucket-b/warehouse",
+      "jdbc-driver": "org.postgresql.Driver"
+    }
+  }'
+
+# 2. Create catalog-a (cust type — mirrors catalog-b)
+curl -X POST http://localhost:8090/api/metalakes/my_metalake/catalogs \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{
+    "name": "catalog-a",
+    "type": "RELATIONAL",
+    "provider": "lakehouse-cust",
+    "comment": "COW mirror of catalog-b",
+    "properties": {
+      "upstream-catalog": "catalog-b",
+      "uri": "jdbc:postgresql://db:5432/iceberg_a",
+      "warehouse": "s3://bucket-a/warehouse",
+      "jdbc-driver": "org.postgresql.Driver"
+    }
+  }'
+```
+
+### Configuration Properties
+
+| Property | Required | Description |
+|---|---|---|
+| `upstream-catalog` | **Yes** | Name of the upstream Iceberg catalog (catalog-b) in the same metalake. |
+| `uri` | **Yes** | JDBC connection URI for catalog-a's metadata store. |
+| `warehouse` | **Yes** | catalog-a's warehouse path (where materialized table data/metadata is stored). |
+| `jdbc-driver` | **Yes** | JDBC driver class name (e.g. `org.postgresql.Driver`, `org.sqlite.JDBC`). |
+| `jdbc-user` | No | JDBC username (if required by the backend). |
+| `jdbc-password` | No | JDBC password (if required by the backend). |
+| `iceberg-jdbc-schema-version` | No | JDBC schema version (`V1` recommended for view support). Default: `V1`. |
+| `iceberg-jdbc-strict-mode` | No | If `true`, requires explicit namespace creation. Default: `false`. |
+
+> **Note**: The `catalog-backend` property is forced to `cust` internally; any user-supplied value
+> is overwritten with a warning.
+
+## Table States
+
+Every table visible through catalog-a is in one of three states:
+
+### 1. UNMATERIALIZED\_MIRROR
+
+The table exists **only** in catalog-b. Reads are transparently served from the upstream with the
+metadata location rewritten to catalog-a's warehouse. No local JDBC entry exists.
+
+- `loadTable`: returns upstream metadata with rewritten location
+- `metadataLocation`: returns `null` (no local entry)
+- Writes: trigger **first-write materialization** (see below)
+
+### 2. MATERIALIZED
+
+The table has been materialized — a local JDBC entry exists and the data files have been copied
+(as part of the client's write operation). The table is now **fully decoupled** from the upstream.
+
+- `loadTable`: returns local metadata (upstream is never consulted)
+- `metadataLocation`: returns the JDBC-stored metadata location
+- Writes: go through the standard JdbcCatalog commit path
+
+### 3. LOCAL\_ONLY
+
+The table was created directly in catalog-a via `CREATE TABLE` (not through materialization). It
+has no upstream counterpart.
+
+- Same behavior as MATERIALIZED, but was never an upstream mirror.
+
+## First-Write Materialization
+
+When a client writes to an UNMATERIALIZED\_MIRROR table:
+
+1. The client loads the table via `loadTable` (gets `CustTableOperations`).
+2. The client performs the write (e.g. `AppendFiles`).
+3. `CustTableOperations.commit` delegates to the local JdbcCatalog with `base=null`, triggering
+   the **create-table (INSERT)** code path.
+4. The JDBC `UNIQUE(catalog, namespace, table)` constraint provides the CAS guarantee.
+
+### Concurrent First-Write
+
+If multiple writers race to materialize the same table:
+
+- **Exactly one** writer succeeds (CAS winner).
+- All other writers receive `CommitFailedException` (standard Iceberg conflict signal).
+- Losers should `loadTable` again (which now returns the materialized table) and retry their
+  operation on top of the winner's snapshot.
+
+```java
+// Standard Iceberg retry pattern for concurrent first-write
+while (true) {
+    try {
+        Table table = catalog.loadTable(ident);
+        // ... build append ...
+        table.commit();  // may throw CommitFailedException on CAS loss
+        break;
+    } catch (CommitFailedException e) {
+        // Table was materialized by another writer; reload and retry
+        continue;
+    }
+}
+```
+
+## DDL Behavior
+
+| Operation | Behavior |
+|---|---|
+| `CREATE TABLE` | Rejected if the table exists locally **or** upstream. Prevents shadowing catalog-b tables. |
+| `DROP TABLE` | Drops from catalog-a only. Rejected with `ForbiddenException` if the table is an unmaterialized mirror (nothing local to drop). `purge=true` only affects catalog-a's warehouse. |
+| `RENAME TABLE` | Only on materialized/local tables. Rejected with `ForbiddenException` on unmaterialized mirrors. |
+| `CREATE/DROP VIEW` | Standard local catalog behavior; does not participate in mirroring. |
+| `LIST NAMESPACES` | Union of local and upstream namespaces. |
+| `LOAD NAMESPACE` | Local properties for local namespaces; empty virtual properties for upstream-only. |
+| `DROP NAMESPACE` | Local only; rejected for upstream-only virtual namespaces. |
+
+## Metrics
+
+The cust catalog registers four counters under
+`gravitino-catalog.cust.<catalog-name>`:
+
+| Metric | Description |
+|---|---|
+| `cust.mirror.reads` | Number of `loadTable` calls that fell through to the upstream. |
+| `cust.materialize.events` | Number of successful first-write materializations. |
+| `cust.conflict.counts` | Number of concurrent first-write CAS conflicts. |
+| `cust.upstream.fwd.reads` | Number of reads forwarded to the upstream (mirrors `mirror.reads`). |
+
+## Audit Events
+
+The cust catalog publishes three event types to the Gravitino `EventBus`:
+
+| Event | Operation Type | When |
+|---|---|---|
+| `CustMirrorReadEvent` | `LOAD_TABLE` | Unmaterialized mirror table loaded from upstream. |
+| `CustMaterializeEvent` | `CREATE_TABLE` | First-write materialization succeeded. Carries `metadata-location` in `customInfo`. |
+| `CustConflictEvent` | `CREATE_TABLE` / `FAILURE` | Concurrent first-write CAS conflict lost. |
+
+All events carry:
+- `EventSource.GRAVITINO_ICEBERG_REST_SERVER`
+- `customInfo`: `catalog-type=cust`, `catalog-name=<name>`, `iceberg-table=<ident>`
+
+## Operations: Orphan File Cleanup
+
+Unmaterialized mirror reads do not write any files to catalog-a's warehouse. After a table is
+materialized, subsequent commits produce standard Iceberg metadata/data files under catalog-a's
+warehouse path.
+
+To clean up orphan files (expired snapshots, stale metadata):
+
+```sql
+-- In Spark with the catalog-a configured
+ALTER TABLE catalog-a.ns.tbl EXECUTE REMOVE_ORPHAN_FILES;
+```
+
+This uses Iceberg's standard `remove-orphan-files` procedure and only affects files under
+catalog-a's warehouse. It never touches catalog-b's storage.
+
+## Module Structure
+
+```
+catalog-lakehouse-cust/
+├── src/main/java/.../cust/
+│   ├── CustCatalog.java                    # Gravitino catalog plugin (SPI entry point)
+│   ├── CustCatalogOperations.java          # Plugin ops; wires upstream lookup + observability
+│   ├── CustCatalogPropertiesMetadata.java  # Property definitions + transformProperties
+│   ├── CustIcebergCatalog.java             # Iceberg Catalog: loadTable/tableExists/listTables/DDL
+│   ├── CustTableOperations.java            # TableOperations for unmaterialized mirror + commit
+│   ├── CustMetadataRewriter.java           # Rewrites upstream metadata location to local warehouse
+│   ├── GravitinoEnvUpstreamLookup.java     # Production upstream resolver via CatalogManager
+│   ├── UpstreamLookup.java                 # Interface for upstream resolution
+│   ├── UpstreamLookupHolder.java           # Static holder (side-channel injection)
+│   ├── CustObservability.java              # Per-catalog metrics + events facade
+│   ├── CustObservabilityHolder.java        # Static holder for MetricsSystem + EventBus
+│   ├── CustMetricsSource.java              # 4 counters: mirror.reads, materialize, conflict, fwd
+│   ├── CustEvent.java                      # Abstract base for cust events
+│   ├── CustMirrorReadEvent.java            # Mirror read event
+│   ├── CustMaterializeEvent.java           # Materialization event
+│   └── CustConflictEvent.java              # CAS conflict event
+├── src/test/java/.../cust/
+│   ├── TestCustCatalog.java                # Catalog plugin tests
+│   ├── TestCustCatalogOperations.java      # Operations tests
+│   ├── TestCustCatalogPropertiesMetadata.java
+│   ├── TestCustMetadataRewriter.java       # Location rewriting tests
+│   ├── TestCustIcebergCatalog.java         # Routing override tests
+│   ├── TestCustCommit.java                 # First-write materialization + CAS tests
+│   ├── TestCustDdl.java                    # DDL/namespace/view tests
+│   ├── TestCustMetrics.java                # Counter verification
+│   └── TestCustEvents.java                 # EventBus event verification
+└── build.gradle.kts
+```
